<title>AUSTRALIA: Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in last year.</title>
<headline>Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in last year.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a list of the 10 largest gaining and falling stocks for Australian companies included in the Australian Stock Exchange's ASX 100 index for the year to June 6.</p>
<p>Top 10 largest gains in year</p>
<p>Rank Name		    Price   pct change</p>
<p> 1   Oil Search	     3.46   166.15</p>
<p> 2   Sthn Pac Pete	  4.70   146.07</p>
<p> 3   CSL Limited	    8.26    67.21</p>
<p> 4   Howard Smith	  12.40    66.22</p>
<p> 5   Wesfarmers	    11.90    64.14</p>
<p> 6   Natl Aust Bank	18.77    62.37</p>
<p> 7   A N Z Bank	     9.09    61.17</p>
<p> 8   Hardie Inds	    4.05    60.08</p>
<p> 9   Transurban Group   990.00    59.68</p>
<p>10   Aust Gas Light	 7.89    55.93</p>
<p>Top 10 largest falls in year</p>
<p>Rank Name		    Price   pct change</p>
<p> 1   Newcrest Mining	3.27   -40.87</p>
<p> 2   Acacia Resources     1.94   -40.85</p>
<p> 3   Sons Of Gwalia	 5.40   -40.00</p>
<p> 4   Davids Limited	 1.25   -32.43</p>
<p> 5   Great Central	  2.58   -31.20</p>
<p> 6   Plutonic Rsc	   4.75   -31.16</p>
<p> 7   Goldfields	     2.16   -29.18</p>
<p> 8   Normandy Min	   1.63   -24.54</p>
<p> 9   News Corp-Prefd	4.76   -21.19</p>
<p>10   Village Road-Pr	3.28   -19.01</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
